[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
### What happened?

`mapbox-gl-js` v2 introduced the **Free-Camera API** (`map.getFreeCameraOptions()`, `map.setFreeCameraOptions()`, `FreeCameraOptions`).  
MapLibre GL JS never shipped those methods – it forked from Mapbox GL JS v1.13, so the free-camera calls simply don’t exist.  

When you migrated you probably kept the same code:

```js
// Mapbox v2
map.setFreeCameraOptions({
  position: [lng, lat, altitude],   // metres above sea level
  bearing: 45,
  pitch: 60,
  roll: 0
});
```

After the swap to MapLibre this throws:

```
map.setFreeCameraOptions is not a function
```

That’s **not** a mistake in the migration steps; it’s a missing API that has to be replaced with the MapLibre equivalent.

---

## 1️⃣ Replace the Free-Camera calls with the MapLibre workflow

MapLibre provides a **calculator** that turns a “camera-style” description (lng/lat/alt + bearing/pitch/roll) into a normal `CameraOptions` object (`center`, `zoom`, `pitch`, `bearing`, `elevation`, `roll`).  
You then feed that object to any of the standard camera methods (`jumpTo`, `easeTo`, `flyTo`).

### Step-by-step code

```js
// -------------------------------------------------
// 1️⃣  Import / instantiate MapLibre (already done)
// -------------------------------------------------
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2
});

// -------------------------------------------------
// 2️⃣  When you need to position the camera at a
//     specific lng/lat/altitude, use the calculator
// -------------------------------------------------
async function setCameraAt(lng, lat, altitudeMeters, {
  bearing = 0,
  pitch = 0,
  roll = 0,
  zoom   // optional – if omitted the calculator derives a zoom that fits the altitude
} = {}) {
  // The calculator returns a full CameraOptions object
  const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
    [lng, lat],          // lng/lat
    altitudeMeters,      // altitude in metres above sea level
    bearing,             // degrees clockwise from north
    pitch,               // degrees
    roll                 // degrees
  );

  // If you want a smooth transition, use easeTo / flyTo
  // For an instant jump, use jumpTo
  map.jumpTo(camOpts);   // or map.easeTo(camOpts) / map.flyTo(camOpts)
}

// -------------------------------------------------
// 3️⃣  Call it wherever you used the old API
// -------------------------------------------------
setCameraAt(-122.42, 37.78, 500, {
  bearing: 45,
  pitch:   60,
  roll:    0
});
```

**Key points**

| Mapbox v2 method | MapLibre replacement | What it does |
|------------------|----------------------|--------------|
| `map.setFreeCameraOptions(opts)` | `const cam = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(lngLat, altitude, bearing, pitch, roll); map.jumpTo(cam)` | Converts a “camera” description to a normal `CameraOptions` and moves the view. |
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` | No direct getter. You can read the current `map.getCenter()`, `map.getZoom()`, `map.getPitch()`, `map.getBearing()`, `map.getElevation()` (v5+) and `map.getRoll()` (v5+). | If you need the current camera state, query those individual getters. |
| `FreeCameraOptions` class | Not present. Use the plain object returned by the calculator. | The object contains `{center, zoom, bearing, pitch, elevation, roll}`. |

---

## 2️⃣ Other migration steps you should double-check

Even if the free-camera issue is the blocker you’re seeing, a complete migration usually requires a few more things. If any of these are still using the old Mapbox values you’ll hit other errors (blank map, 401, missing methods, etc.).

| What to verify | How to fix |
|----------------|------------|
| **Package & import** | `npm uninstall mapbox-gl && npm install maplibre-gl`  <br> `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` |
| **Namespace** | Replace every `mapboxgl` with `maplibregl`. |
| **Access token** | Remove `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. MapLibre does **not** need a token. |
| **Style URL** | `style: 'mapbox://…'` → a non-Mapbox URL (e.g. OpenFreeMap, your own TileJSON, a PMTiles URL, etc.). |
| **CSS class names** | `mapboxgl-` → `maplibregl-` (controls, popups, etc.). |
| **Callbacks → promises** | Methods like `map.loadImage`, `source.getClusterChildren`, `source.getClusterLeaves`, `source.getClusterExpansionZoom` now return a `Promise`. Convert `await map.loadImage(url)` or `.then(...)`. |
| **v2-only APIs** | `map.setFog` → `map.setSky`. <br> `map.setTerrain` and `map.setProjection` still exist with the same names. |
| **Plugins** | - `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw` works after you change its CSS constants (or switch to `terra-draw`). <br> - `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` → `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`. <br> - `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-directions` → `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-directions`. <br> - `mapbox-gl-compare` → `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-compare`. |
| **Tile source wiring** | If you kept a Mapbox style JSON, replace every `source` URL that starts with `mapbox://` (tiles, sprites, glyphs) with URLs that point to your new provider. Use **Maputnik** or the CLI `gl-style-validate` to catch stray `mapbox://` references. |
| **WebGL2 requirement** | MapLibre v6+ requires WebGL2. If you need to support older browsers, pin to a v5.x release (`npm install maplibre-gl@5`). |

