## 1️⃣ @mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw  →  drawing shapes

| What you have | What you need to change | Why it works / why you might want an alternative |
|---------------|------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| `import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw'` | **Keep the same import** (the package still works) | The library only talks to the MapLibre API (`Map`, `Marker`, `Popup`, `addSource`, `addLayer`, …). It does **not** depend on any Mapbox-only service. |
| `new MapboxDraw({ … })` | No code change needed | The constructor expects a `map` instance that implements the MapLibre `Map` interface – which it does. |
| CSS classes in your own stylesheet (`.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-…`) | Rename the prefix to `maplibregl-` **or** keep the old class names if you import the default draw CSS. | The draw CSS file ships with selectors that use the `mapboxgl-` prefix. When you load that CSS the selectors still match the DOM because the elements still have the old class names (`mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-…`). If you write custom overrides you must change the prefix. |
| Custom styling (e.g. `button.mapboxgl-ctrl-draw-polygon`) | Change to `button.maplibregl-ctrl-draw-polygon` (or keep the old selector if you keep the original CSS) | MapLibre’s own controls use the `maplibregl-` prefix, so any UI you add that mixes with the draw controls should use the same naming scheme. |
| Using the **“draw”** control | ```js\nimport MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw';\nimport '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw/dist/mapbox-gl-draw.css';\n\nconst draw = new MapboxDraw({\n  displayControlsDefault: false,\n  controls: { polygon: true, trash: true }\n});\nmap.addControl(draw);\n``` | No further changes. |
| **Optional** – you want a plugin that already ships with the `maplibregl-` prefix | Use **Terra Draw** (`terra-draw` + `terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter`). It is a community-maintained fork that ships with MapLibre-styled CSS and a few extra tools (snapping, measurement, etc.). | If you prefer a “MapLibre-first” package, install it: `npm i terra-draw terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter` and replace the import with `import { TerraDrawMapLibreGLAdapter } from 'terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter';` – see the Terra Draw README for a quick start. |

### Quick sanity-check after the swap

```js
map.on('load', () => {
  // draw should be ready
  console.log('draw mode?', draw.getMode()); // → 'simple_select' (default)
});
```

If the draw UI appears but the buttons are unstyled, double-check that the CSS file from `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw` is being loaded **after** the MapLibre CSS (order matters).

