## 2️⃣ @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder  →  search box

Mapbox-GL-Geocoder is tightly coupled to the Mapbox Geocoding API (it injects the access token, builds the request URL, and expects Mapbox-specific response fields). You must replace it with a **MapLibre-compatible** version and point it at an open geocoder service.

### 2.1 Install the MapLibre fork

```bash
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
# also install a geocoder backend of your choice, e.g. Nominatim:
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder-nominatim   # optional helper package
```

> **Why a fork?** The fork removes the hard-coded Mapbox token handling and lets you supply any endpoint that follows the Mapbox Geocoding response schema (or a compatible one). It also renames the CSS prefix to `maplibregl-`.

### 2.2 Import & CSS

```js
// MapLibre core
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';

// Geocoder (MapLibre fork)
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';
```

### 2.3 Choose a backend

| Backend | URL pattern (example) | Notes |
|--------|-----------------------|-------|
| **Nominatim (public)** | `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&addressdetails=1&q={query}` | Free for low-volume testing only. Must include `User-Agent`/`Referer` header per OSM policy. |
| **Photon** | `https://photon.komoot.io/api/?q={query}` | Returns GeoJSON-compatible results. |
| **MapTiler Geocoding** | `https://api.maptiler.com/geocoding/{query}.json?key=YOUR_KEY` | Requires a MapTiler API key (free tier available). |
| **Self-hosted Nominatim / Pelias / OpenCage** | Your own endpoint | Best for production. |

The MapLibre-Geocoder package expects the **response to be in the Mapbox Geocoding format** (or a format you tell it to parse). The easiest way is to use the **helper package** that adapts Nominatim/Photon responses:

```bash
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder-nominatim
```

```js
import { NominatimGeocoder } from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder-nominatim';

const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // No accessToken property – you don’t need it
  placeholder: 'Search places …',
  // Use the helper that converts Nominatim → Mapbox format
  geocoder: new NominatimGeocoder({
    // optional: limit results, language, etc.
    endpoint: 'https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search',
    // you can add extra query params here
    params: { addressdetails: 1, limit: 5 }
  })
});
map.addControl(geocoder);
```

If you prefer to call the service yourself, you can pass a custom `fetch` function:

```js
const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  placeholder: 'Search …',
  // custom fetch that rewrites the response to Mapbox format
  forwardGeocode: async (query) => {
    const resp = await fetch(`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`);
    const data = await resp.json();

    // Convert Nominatim GeoJSON → Mapbox-style feature collection
    const features = data.features.map(f => ({
      type: 'Feature',
      geometry: f.geometry,
      place_name: f.properties.display_name,
      center: f.geometry.coordinates,
      // any other properties you need
    }));

    return { features };
  },
  // optional reverseGeocode if you need it
});
```

### 2.4 Replace the old import / usage

| Old (Mapbox) | New (MapLibre) |
|--------------|----------------|
| `import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder'` | `import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder'` |
| `new MapboxGeocoder({ accessToken: MAPBOX_TOKEN, ... })` | `new MapLibreGeocoder({ /* no token */ ... })` |
| `map.addControl(geocoder)` | Same call, just with the new instance |
| CSS class overrides (`.mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder`) | Use `.maplibregl-ctrl-geocoder` (or keep the old selector if you import the original CSS, but the fork ships its own CSS with the new prefix). |

### 2.5 Remove the Mapbox token completely

```js
// Delete any line like this – it will cause a 401 if left in
// mapboxgl.accessToken = 'pk.ey...';
```

If you still have other Mapbox services (e.g., tiles) you’ll see 401 errors in the console; those belong to step 3 of the overall migration (replace the style URL).

### 2.6 Test the geocoder

```js
geocoder.on('result', (e) => {
  console.log('selected', e.result);
  // e.result is a GeoJSON Feature (Mapbox-style)
  map.flyTo({ center: e.result.center, zoom: 14 });
});
```

If you get a CORS error, make sure the geocoder service you chose sends the appropriate `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header (most public instances do). For self-hosted services you control the headers.

